namespace OpenTPW.UI.Original;

/// <summary>
/// Register of every UI value or rule that is not taken from original data or hard evidence
/// (docs/UI.md "Approximation register"). Each site carries a matching
/// <c>// [APPROX:UI-NNN]</c> comment; <see cref="LogOnce"/> reports them at startup.
/// </summary>
public static class UiApproximations
{
	public static readonly IReadOnlyList<(string Id, string Assumption, string EvidenceNeeded)> All = new[]
	{
		("UI-003", "the state selection of the original UI model draw beyond the stored selected-mesh endpoints is not traced; the instance traverser 0x57a530 composes each node's world matrix from its local matrix and its ancestors' (the root starts as its local matrix times the caller's, the identity set at 0x57a55b being overwritten), OpenTPW does the same, no ui.wad child carries a rotation or scale (only translations, which cancel in the selected-mesh fit), and the window angle (+0xe2) is ported as DrawFrame's turn (0x476c50)", "the UI control draw's selection of a state frame"),
		("UI-004", "UI model triangles drawn back to front by Z, grouped per texture; the original draws a UI model as nodes of the scene instance list: the walker 0x576910 (it sets global 0x8bb624 to 0x1000000 while it walks, which 0x581cd0 reads at 0x581cf6, 0x581cff and 0x581d15) appends their parts through the traverser 0x57a530 and 0x581cd0, and the frame batcher 0x581db0 gives every part its state word from its texture's alpha type (0x581790 -> 0x590c40, so a cut-out interface texture is tested at 0xf0/255 like a world texture), draws the states of bits 0x1000 and 0x2000 at once in file order with depth test and depth write on (decoder 0x567620 bits 0x8000 and 0x800 absent) and defers the others, far to near by the part's average depth (0x5829e0) with their triangles sorted by depth sum (0x565490); a part whose material word has bit 0x2 (state bit 0x800000, no shipped material) is keyed by its index span at 0x58109e instead; the display object's UI depth range is [0, 0.1) in front of [0.1, 0.2) and [0.2, 1) (defaults 0x582db4-0x582dc1), but how a UI vertex's depth reaches it (the transform at 0x87b1d8 +0xc) and whether the UI pass shares or clears the scene's depth buffer are not read, so the depth-tested file order is not ported", "the depth value the UI vertex transform (0x87b1d8 +0xc, called at 0x581092) gives a UI vertex, and whether the depth buffer is cleared between the scene and the UI nodes"),
		("UI-006", "text colours: the object windows' labels and values white, green values elsewhere, a highlight for selected list rows, grey disabled, the texture-switch progress bar track and backdrop colours (the video's 720p chroma is good to about +-15 per channel); the original gives each text control an RGBA colour (0x65c5d5 → renderer +0x48, kept as ARGB at +0x78, 0x48fd07; the sprite draw 0x58a010 takes it as the diffuse colour of the control's quads, 0x58a019), white by default (constructor 0x48f6a0) and with glyphs rendered white (0x48fa96; nothing sets the keep-font-colours flag +0xdd), and all 134 sites are assigned to their window builders in docs/UI.md (text colour sites); the values read and ported are the options labels' (0,0,0,255) (0x4a441e), the buy list rows' (255,255,255,255) (0x4ad340), the pause menu lines' (0,175,190,255) (0x48b2b9), the shared title colour (234,239,102,255) (0x492d20, fifteen window builders), the lobby island name's (252,232,7,255) (0x4b8604), the list column headers' (255,239,0,255) (0x486660, 59 callers), the HUD cost text's (255,255,0,255) (0x4a22b2), the black labels of the park information window (0x4a52a0: title and caption) and ticket price window (0x498d80); the park information window's toggles and period buttons (0x4a52a0) and the finance window's toggles (0x49ac60) are buttons whose SetText override 0x668d5f reapplies white (0x668ad3), the red cost rows' (255,0,0,255) of the hire, training and loans windows (0x49c422, 0x4b2e93, 0x49fce1) and a list row control that turns (140,0,60) on message 0x403 with a negative argument (0x4a0710)", "the list row classes' text, selection and disabled colours behind OpenTPW's Highlight, Value and Disabled, the research fluid cells' (224,86,86) and the other black and red window texts of docs/UI.md that no OpenTPW control draws yet, and the backdrop colours (not 0x65c5d5 sites)"),
		("UI-018", "the lobby draws the engine sky (the scene's one view has the flags 0x1F31, whose bit 0x10 makes 0x576A00 draw the sky in every frame, 0x576C6D; cloud layer sky.tga coloured by the eased island colour) over the fog-coloured clear (render flag 0x4000000, 0x5D8BEA), without fog (the lobby's range 50 to 300 is set but the scene clears the fog bit, 0x5d8bf9; RenderFog, UI-107); while the globe is up the islands screen is deactivated (0x5E23C0 -> 0x5E2550, 0x5E1BD0), which frees the island models, their clips, the flyers and the signs (0x5E25E2, 0x5D8A10), and only active screens update (0x5E40E0), so nothing of the islands component 0x5e0470 (lightning, thunder, rain, the nearest-island sky target) runs and no flyer or clip steps: OpenTPW steps none of them and builds the lobby scene afresh when the globe closes (GameFlow.RebuildLobbyScene, the activation 0x5E23F0 -> 0x5E3210), while the scene keeps easing the sky towards the globe's own target (0x5d96c0, 0x5DCFE0); the enter sequence is built (the camera turns to the island angle + π, the gate plays M1, the camera zooms under the black fade and the park starts below radius 8, 0x5e0490 states 1 and 2) and Escape ends it as the original's handler does (0x5E41C0 -> 0x5E1890, 0x5E2360, the base 0x5e1350: sub-state 0, the opened gate closes with M2, the menu is back); tp.exe's lobby code has no key-award animation: the key panel (0x4B8CA0, 0x4B9340, 0x4B90F0) is a static counter with the sparkle effect 0x61 (LobbyKeyPanelEffect) and a won ticket is a text popup in the park (0x4D4BC0, 0x4D4FA0); the CRT's process-wide rand() stream (the island constructors', the flyers' and the lightning's draws) is replaced by a local clock-seeded stand-in", "whether the rain the islands update held keeps falling behind the globe (the count is read by the weather draw, 0x57efd0), the second islands screen's Escape branch (0x5E2360, [[0x48B390]+0x384]), what the globe screen D (vtable 0x702E20) is for, and the original's rand() stream"),
		("UI-025", "the message tube is the original's tag window system: ten slots, no eviction, no help (the add routine 0x48eb20, cap word 0x750610); every post names a tag whose record (content/data/message-tags.toml, the table 0x75eca8) decides its text entry, replacement, icon, actions and lifetime (30 s for most tags, 90 s for the offers, none for the progress rows; the expiry timer 0x80080 and the warning timer 0x80081 five seconds earlier run on the UI clock, 0x661fe5, and a pause suspends them, 0x48a6e0); a row is kept until it is deleted, answered or expired (0x48d9c0 stops an armed non-offer tag's timers and removes nothing); a deleted, expired or answered row leaves 500 ms later with the decline run first for an offer (0x4a13e8, 0x48db94, 0x48e269); a replaced row leaves at once; a right click on the tag the panel is still sliding out for does nothing (0x7ca094) and one on the tube's body removes every row 100 ms apart (0x4a1190, 0x100003); the panel's buttons come from the tag's actions (buy with its entry preselected, hire, loans, research, park information, staff costs and entry price windows, locate a thing or a cell: 0x48e610, 0x48e0f0); the first show starts the burst 0x5a and the warning the retained particle 0x5b at the icon's centre, ended by a read or the removal (0x48dfbe, 0x48de1a); the tube is saved with the park and an original save's tube is imported (0x48ee50, 0x48ef70); the tube art remains an extension", "the locate actions' operands: the original fills the context words (the advice builder 0x59b590 takes the thing id and the secondary word as its arguments 2 and 3; the scan callbacks leave words at the scan object +4 and +8, which the speech copies into the record when they are not 0, 0x59b6cf-0x59b6e4; they reach the tube through 0x59b7d4 -> 0x40f740 -> 0x509bf0), while OpenTPW's AdvisorController.SpeechCheck returns the score only and the builders pass 0, so a locate button does nothing for our own advice (a follow-up per scan callback), the place of the 0x5a burst (the window's rectangle before the tube positions it, 0x4a12e3, is not read: the icon's centre is used), the icons' bounce animations (tables 0x7502f0 and 0x752e48), and writing the original's own tag block (OpenTPW's resume save keeps its own JSON part)"),
		("UI-026", "build icons: the preview model (P<name>.MD2, else the main model) is drawn depth tested in its own image ([EXT:preview-icon-cpu-projection]) with the original's placement, camera and face test: the fit and footprint terms of 0x4689f0, the matrix 0x468e50 rebuilds each frame (the yaw and the -π/4 tilt through the sine table, the offsets, x scaled by 0.75 and depth by 0.1), the instance's own view diag(1, -1, 1, 1) (0x45bd30, 0x57a260, used for model flag 0x200 by 0x57a750), the viewport mapping with depth × 0.1 (0x579690 mode 2), the clockwise-only face test (0x581320) and LESSEQUAL depth (0x567620, 0x57360f), its turn of 0.0004 rad a millisecond running on across selections (0x46908a, 0x468e2f), and animation 5 started on each new preview (0x4732a0: <model>m1, else <model>m, looping); but the original lights the preview's vertices in its 3D object pipeline and OpenTPW draws them unlit: 0x57aa10 clears the light list 0x879dec, relinks the lights of the scene's two containers ([0x87a6d0] + 0x30 and + 0x2c) through 0x576230 and lights each vertex with 0x574660 → 0x5741b0 (the ambient words 0x879dd8, 0.15 grey by default, 0x573fd0, plus for each directional light, type nibble 2 of +0x50, its colour × max(-N·d, 0) in the model's space, for a point light, 4, (r² - d²) × 1/r², clamped to bytes with alpha 0xFF; the option LIGHTING, bit 0x800 of [0x8bcbc8], takes the unlit colour [+0x2c] instead), which is read; the footprint grid (8×8 cells coloured by cell type in control 0x1eb, 0x4ab1b0, record 0x754d50) is built (BuyFootprint) and its cell rectangles' edges match 0x4ab1b0 (round 11 package I); the object windows' previews keep a 30° tilt and 0.8 rad/s; sign faces use the object's rendered sign textures (ObjectSigns)", "which lights the scene holds while the buy window is open: the advisor adds its own white directional light (0.6, -0.6, 0.2) at 0x429bc9..0x429d15 to the same scene, the light script engine (0x458102, 0x4582d4) adds model lights, and the source of the park's own sun (ThemeEngine.DirectionalLightLevel, LightNormal in the theme's Standard.sam) was not traced to a scene light, so the lit colour of a preview vertex cannot be computed yet"),
		("UI-031", "exactly Ctrl at the placing click keeps the build tool armed (0x5253b8; the Move tool's 0x5259e2), a ride with an entrance takes the queue tool after its placement whatever the modifier (0x52f580(3, 0)), and the queue tool's last click ends the tool whatever the modifier (0x5275b1..0x5275f2: 0x52f200(0, 0) sets mode 0 and replaces the build tool object, its mode 4 or 0x3b with its type, by the default tool), the tool's angle returning to 0 when it is left (0x52f3b6); the kart and water line tools (0xB, 0x10) take the queue tool when their circuit closes only while the placement's queue start 0x8186c0 is pending (0x526f95, 0x527004), from the cell the last placement stored (0x7639b8/0x7639bc), and the handover takes it (0x527056), as build and Move clicks on an accepted ghost (a click on a refused ghost returns at the latch first, 0x524a63), the Move pick-up and path or queue commits drop it (0x524b53, 0x5253f3, 0x525e5a, 0x527483), a path start cell ending the queue tool at once (0x52712f), and with no queue start exactly Ctrl keeps the line tool without a start (0x527146) and any other word ends it (0x527156); the Ctrl word 0xC at 0x5259e2/0x5259f4 is Ctrl alone (the modifier builder 0x46b420: Shift 3, Ctrl 0xC, Alt 0x30) and a placement that 0x52fab0 reports as entrance-bearing (the sub-record flag +0x40) takes the tail 0x5259ae: the queue re-evaluation 0x4de1f0, the words 0x763ac0 and 0x763ac4 back to 0x80, then the map cell record +0x29c (the cell's type word, +8 of the 0x44-byte record at +0x294) of the queue's start cell that 0x52a050 gave decides at 0x5259cf: type 1 (a path cell) ends the tool through 0x52f200(0, 0) whatever the modifier, which returns the angle to 0 as well (0x52f3b6); for any other start cell the mode stays the queue tool 3 that 0x52f580 set before, exactly Ctrl keeps the angle through it (0x525a06) and any other word runs 0x52f1b0(0, 0), which resets it (OpenTPW keeps the angle through the queue tool whatever the modifier and