5 with the flag 0x820abc, which 0x5345ad sets only while the last-cell word 0x820ab8 is nonzero (the gate at 0x534584..0x534593) and the cell is a path or queue cell), which takes 0x526568, and any other result falls to 0x526527; which of OpenTPW's placements have a path cell as the queue's start"),
		("UI-042", "the camera button's slide-out panel (table 0x751720) slides in and out as the arm drawer 0x4a14f0 does (ten 20 ms steps, cat_ui 0x1C and 0xC2, help 0x131): the drawer places the panel at the arm's left less the panel's own width and a horizontal gap of 50 (0x4a1631, the width read by 0x659e3e), centred vertically on the arm (the arm's top plus half the arm's height less half the panel's, 0x4a163b-0x4a1647) and then moves it right by a tenth of (the HUD window's right edge - the arm's left + the panel's width + 100) each step (0x4a16e5, the step 0x4a1704, the tick 0x4a19e7), the step being the integer quotient by the tick count 10 and the ten ticks adding it, so the panel ends at its start plus 10 times that step (the camera panel at left 482, top 1206; the message panel through the same drawer at left 486, top 1112) with the arm's art (bar, pane and handle) growing out from under the HUD; the camcorder button arms the camcorder tool as the C key does (button 99, 0x498ad0 → 0x481a10 → the tool 0x46cff0, vtable 0x6fead0), and the tool's click (0x46d0d0, on the press) boards the ride under the cursor or starts the walk (0x42ae70): the camera update 0x42b1c0 in mode 2 with the original's keys (the arrows and numpad 1, 3, 7, 9), pointer steering, cell-edge stepping with the mask-2 walk test (0x4d8750) and eye (ground + 5 units), matched to the executable by an x86 oracle (ORACLE.md X58); the postcard window (table 0x7540d8) keeps its photo frame empty and its preview button disabled (the 640×240 camcorder photo 0x4a9280 and the preview redraw 0x4a84c0 are not ported); its address book (table 0x7542b8, 0x4a8140) and its sending through OpenTPW's own server are not part of this ID ([EXT:online-postcard-address-book], user-approved 2026-10-30); the original has no view-cycle button, so OpenTPW has none (0x751720 holds only the two buttons; no window control changes the zoom or yaw, and the locate jumps 0x42aab0 pass null zoom and yaw)", "the photo and its preview; host rule: a lost window focus or a pointer outside the window drops the walk's keys and pointer offset (the walker still coasts on its velocity, 0x42b1c0)"),
		("UI-060", "finance and park information share the original's graph drawer 0x47fe90: the opaque black backdrop, dark-green grid (0,100,0), green axes/step labels (0,200,0), plot (4,4,width-20,height-20), ten horizontal divisions and twelve labeled vertical spans for 12/36/144 samples (0x4806a0, 0x47fb50, 0x47fcd0), the series colours/order, selection masks, default bank balance and zero-inclusive scale, and the finance series' placement: n = min(period samples, months held) + 1 points from the left over steps of width / samples (floats summed as the drawer does), a 0 before the first month while the ring has no older one, whole-pixel columns and rows cut to the plot, a box round each segment end below 144 samples and the last value at the line's end (0x480460, 0x47fe90, 0x47ffe0); grid coordinates accumulate stored floats and truncate, primitive lengths are pixel counts (the pixel size itself, two canvas units and at least one framebuffer pixel, is the host adapter [EXT:graph-pixel-adapter], user-approved 2026-10-30, and the graph label font follows [EXT:ui-font-tier-by-scale]), and the negative-minimum zero axis omits the bottom branch's extra pixel (0x47fc50). Empty histories and selections keep the backdrop. Signed 128-bit axis and row arithmetic for long financial values (the original multiplies in 32 bits, 0x47feee), background-only tiny/unsupported host controls and nonfinite-frame rejection are host safety adaptations", "the original's 32-bit wrap of a financial span above about 8.9 million (OpenTPW draws the true value); a rendered composition of the graphs against the original's raster"),
		("UI-082", "the hire figure uses the traced inner rectangle, integer feet (626,362) and nominal 2.4 canvas units per reference pixel; it is the script's own sprite (0x74F758: flags 0x51000 and heading 5 by its SET instructions, slot 1, frames 0 to 7) made by 0x49BA00 at the sprite clock and stepped by the sprite scheduler on the even substeps (0x475360, 0x54F5D7): a new role or variant byte starts a figure that shows nothing before the first due pass (62 ms, strictly later, 0x4758F0), an applicant the pool does not return keeps the figure that stands, and the window's close ends it (0x49B7B4); the screen-space draw takes no camera turn (flag 0x40000); the employed-tab figure deliberately shares the hire-box layout as EXT:staff-employee-view, not native applicant sourcing", "the control depth word (+0xE0, the z register 0x476A70) and exact viewport/raster parity with the original's sprite pass"),
		("UI-086", "the map window's cells, layers, items, tracks and pointer follow tp.exe 0x5f2050 (the class writer: cells 10, 11 and 12 for paths, queues and unowned land, 9 for a fence post, structure type 0x19 (0x536450), the class of the owner thing for an object cell, 0x4dd4e0 +0x4ac), 0x5f2380 (the renderer: the layer word, the staff role and the value mode, the 5 × 5 pixel grid from (15, 42), the fills and the outline pass 0x5f2a94 (with its cell-width quirk) blended with the alpha of their colour (out = d + ((s - d) * a >> 8), 0x5f23cd, so an opaque fill still loses 1 where it is above the base), the staff areas as one pixel frames (0x6025c0, each pixel once, alpha 200) and the coaster track polylines through the anti-aliased line 0x5efb10, oracle X54), 0x5f3940 and 0x5f44d0 (the six sprite images, the item filters, the colour kinds, the staff patrol areas, the happiness ramp 0x5f09a0 and the repair, excitement 0x4e0860 and satisfaction 0x4e1e30 value modes) and the pointer's nearest-item pick within five pixels with its text panel; 0x5f2fd0 is the track layer (called at 0x5f2d99 under layer bit 0x10), and the pointer pick is 0x5f198e..0x5f1a96 (|dx| and |dy| below 5.0, 0x703040); not ported: the sprite size follows the display height in the original (the quad is the image width × the item scale × 0.00078125 of the display height) and OpenTPW uses the 640 × 480 reference size, as for the pick's 5 pixel radius, which is in screen pixels of the original's display mode; the surface's pixel format: the original takes its D3D format from the table 0x8bd558[[0x8bd554]] (A4R4G4B4 when the option TEXTURE32, bit 0x400000 of [0x7a1a8c], is 0, as in its default presets, else A8R8G8B8: 0x5f1f81..0x5f1fcc, 0x44e1eb..0x44e202; the software renderer forces 8888, 0x58daca), and OpenTPW's textures are always 32 bit (GraphicalOptions.TEXTURE32 is not applied, docs/COMPATIBILITY.md), so the 4444 surface (a 16 bpp surface: the original draws its fills, outlines and frames with the 16 bit drawer, vtable 0x703680 set at 0x617390, as well as the line) and the 8, 16 and 24 bit line variants (0x5edad0, 0x5ee580, 0x5ef040, jump table 0x5f3218) are not ported; whether the item colour modulates or replaces the sprite texel; the pointer's click-through, drag pan and camera-centred initial view and the hover text beyond the item's name; and a per-pixel comparison with a capture of the original", "the sprite size follows the display height in the original (the quad is the image width × the item scale × 0.00078125 of the display height) and OpenTPW uses the 640 × 480 reference size, as for the pick's 5 pixel radius, which is in screen pixels of the original's display mode; the surface's pixel format: the original takes its D3D format from the table 0x8bd558[[0x8bd554]] (A4R4G4B4 when the option TEXTURE32, bit 0x400000 of [0x7a1a8c], is 0, as in its default presets, else A8R8G8B8: 0x5f1f81..0x5f1fcc, 0x44e1eb..0x44e202; the software renderer forces 8888, 0x58daca), and OpenTPW's textures are always 32 bit (GraphicalOptions.TEXTURE32 is not applied, docs/COMPATIBILITY.md), so the 4444 surface (a 16 bpp surface: the original draws its fills, outlines and frames with the 16 bit drawer, vtable 0x703680 set at 0x617390, as well as the line) and the 8, 16 and 24 bit line variants (0x5edad0, 0x5ee580, 0x5ef040, jump table 0x5f3218) are not ported; whether the item colour modulates or replaces the sprite texel; the pointer's click-through, drag pan and camera-centred initial view and the hover text beyond the item's name; and a per-pixel comparison with a capture of the original"),
